# Byte-compiled / cache
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.so

# Generated results - committed because they ARE the deliverable. Never hand-edit them;
# re-run the modules to regenerate (see README "How to run").
# The source clip and the derived crops stay out: they are large and reproducible.

# Real footage and calibration - large, and reproduced from the dataset / your own capture
data/conveyor.mp4
data/zerowaste/
data/zerowaste_gt/
data/zerowaste_crops/
# NB: this also hides the locally generated checkerboard_9x6.png. That is intended -
# the .pdf is committed, and tools/make_checkerboard.py regenerates the .png.
data/checkerboard/*.png
data/checkerboard/*.jpg
!data/checkerboard/checkerboard_9x6.pdf
module_B_calibration/calibration.npz
module_E_recognition/crops/

